00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:17.180
April 11th, 2020, was, as much as one can
be at the moment, a day like any other.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.920
As the U.S. passed half a million cases of
coronavirus, no one paid much attention to

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.429
the unremarkable news in North Korea.

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:30.160
The state-run Korean Central News Agency published
a relatively mundane story about Kim Jong-Un

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.530
attending a Workers’ Party meeting, where
this photo was taken.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.920
What no one knew is that this would be the
last appearance by the Supreme Leader for

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.180
almost three weeks.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.250
After missing his grandfather’s birthday
celebration on Wednesday, something he had

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:51.120
never done in his nine years in power, it
became clear something was up, and the rumors

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.460
began.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.440
On Monday, the South-Korean website Daily
NK reported that Un was recovering from a

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.090
cardiovascular operation, quoting anonymous
sources.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.000
Then, CNN ran the headline “U.S.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.200
Source: North Korean leader in grave danger
after surgery.”, turning the regional report

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.120
into a global story.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:17.390
Soon, an MSNBC anchor with 700,000 followers
tweeted the news, and a media executive posted

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:21.179
two candles on her Weibo page - adding more
fuel to the fire.

00:01:21.179 --> 00:01:26.700
An old picture of Kim Jong-Il’s body, photoshopped
with the face of his son, began circulating

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:31.360
online, along with a video of Chinese military
vehicles supposedly rushing to the border

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.229
- which was later identified as being filmed
further south in Jiangsu.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:42.409
A South Korean lawmaker, one of only two born
in the North, gave his death a 99% probability,

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:46.819
U.S. Senator Lindsey Graham said he would
be “shocked if he’s not dead or in some

00:01:46.819 --> 00:01:51.810
incapacitated state”, and one of the South’s
three major newspapers published an article

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.069
formally announcing the death.

00:01:54.069 --> 00:01:58.580
And if one needed any further confirmation,
Reuters reported Beijing had dispatched a

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.209
team of medical experts to advise on the situation.

00:02:02.209 --> 00:02:07.380
During this time, the South’s National Intelligence
Service repeatedly denied anything unusual

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.160
was going on.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:15.080
As panic turned to confusion, and confusion
turned to skepticism, the original Daily NK

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.830
story issued a correction: it was, actually,
based only on a single, unnamed source.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:25.860
CNN changed its headline to sound more cautious,
and the previously mentioned tweet and post

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.510
were deleted.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:32.440
For a week or so, the media boldly asserted
“he’s either dead… or alive”.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:38.890
Then, on May 1st, 20 days after his last appearance,
Kim Jong-Un returned.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:49.320
This time, to inspect a fertilizer factory
outside Pyongyang.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.440
In hindsight, it’s no secret how these rumors
spread.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.510
“He had a procedure” became “He’s
in critical condition after surgery” became

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.180
“He’s dead” through a series of sloppy
journalistic escalations.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.890
Because so many outlets published the story,
people thought, there must be some truth to

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:07.890
it.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.230
After all, this is perhaps the easiest rumor
to sell.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:17.090
Who would doubt 5-foot, 7”, 300 pound, chain-smoking
Kim Jong-Un - the man who had a harder time

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:22.820
planting a tree in his 30s than his 65-year-old
South Korean counterpart - would have health

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.080
troubles?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.630
Of course, nothing that happened on May 1st
or since precludes the possibility of Kim

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.290
having surgery.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.670
Some medical experts argue a new small mark
seen on the leader’s right wrist could be

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:37.270
a sign of a cardiovascular procedure.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:43.120
He was also seen using a golf cart, as he
did after a 6-week absence in 2014 caused

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.920
by a suspected ankle injury.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.970
Although, he has used the cart at other times
as well.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.230
Another theory suggests Kim may have been
hiding from an outbreak of coronavirus.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.980
Pyongyang residents have reportedly been rushing
to stock up at grocery stores.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.240
Confounding the problem is the current lack
of foreigners in the country and minimal travel

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:07.500
across the Chinese border - making reliable
sources difficult to find.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.400
We may never know why Kim Jong-Un disappeared.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:16.889
What we do know is that the North Korean government
chose not to report on, or snap a photo of

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:20.569
their leader’s whereabouts during those
three weeks.

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:25.650
Whatever the cause of the disappearance, the
strategic reason for silence is simple: After

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:30.099
the world finishes celebrating the death of
a brutal, murderous dictator, it realizes

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:35.780
the somehow even scarier potential alternative:
the subsequent chaotic struggle for control

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:38.920
of its nuclear and chemical weapons.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:43.620
Rumors of Kim’s death are an accidental
reminder of how bad things could be, and how

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.659
much stability is worth.

00:04:45.659 --> 00:04:52.009
So, while recent events may have only been
a false alarm, they invite a very real question.

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:57.090
One day, possibly any day, Kim Jong-Un will
die or be replaced.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:01.710
And when that happens, who will inherit the
nuclear codes?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:09.370
In its 71 years of existence, only three people
and one family have ever ruled the Democratic

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.740
People’s Republic of Korea.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.300
From the country’s founding in 1948, Kim
Il-Sung would stay in power for another 46

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.460
years, until his death in ‘94.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:26.100
During this time, Japan cycled through 21
Prime Ministers, Britain, 11, and the U.S.,

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.169
9 presidents.

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:33.240
The small hermit kingdom would both outlive
its Soviet ally and survive Chinese reform.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:38.489
Around the age of 60, the country’s founder
and then-only leader began planning his legacy

00:05:38.489 --> 00:05:42.800
- first considering his brother, before deciding
on his son.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:47.460
The North Korean dictionary quietly changed
its definition of ‘hereditary succession’

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:52.129
as “a reactionary custom of exploitative
societies” and began distributing paintings

00:05:52.129 --> 00:05:55.620
depicting the leader in a more loving, fatherly
light.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:00.590
For the next few decades, the favored, eldest
son Kim Jong-Il began climbing the party’s

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:06.479
ranks - eventually pronounced Supreme Commander
of the Korean People’s Army in 1991.

00:06:06.479 --> 00:06:11.779
Thanks to this preparation, when a heart attack
killed Kim Il-Sung in 1994, power was smoothly

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:16.560
inherited by his son - becoming the first
hereditary transfer of power in a Communist

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.809
country.

00:06:17.809 --> 00:06:22.550
The question of who would follow Kim Jong-Il
was far more complicated.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:28.710
He first married, on his father’s request,
in 1966 and had a daughter two years later.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.460
One year after that, they divorced, and Kim,
almost immediately, and in secret, found a

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.520
second woman, with whom he had a son - Kim
Jong-Nam.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:42.199
Three years later, not knowing of this second
relationship or child, Kim Jong-Il’s father

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:44.550
instructed him to re-marry another woman.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.779
He did and together the couple had two daughters.

00:06:47.779 --> 00:06:53.339
Finally, a few years later, he met a young
dancer with whom he had a daughter, Yo-Jong,

00:06:53.339 --> 00:06:56.889
and two sons, Jong-Chol and Jong-Un.

00:06:56.889 --> 00:07:01.749
Kim Jong-Il kept each family in separate,
walled-in residences in Pyongyang - giving

00:07:01.749 --> 00:07:07.020
the children quiet and very isolated lives
where they would not encounter each other.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:11.509
When it came time for boarding school, Jong-Nam
was sent to Geneva, while the youngest three

00:07:11.509 --> 00:07:13.430
went to Bern.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.300
What happened next is somewhat disputed.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:20.659
Conventional wisdom says that Kim Jong-Nam,
as the eldest son, was his father’s favorite

00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:26.660
and next in line for the throne, until May
2001, when he was caught sneaking into Japan

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:32.190
to visit Tokyo Disney with a fake Dominican
Republic passport and Chinese name.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:37.499
In truth, the Tokyo incident was likely just
one more straw on the camel’s back - reinforcing

00:07:37.499 --> 00:07:40.039
what was already becoming true.

00:07:40.039 --> 00:07:44.960
In fact, some doubt Disney was the real reason
for the trip, or even suggest the arrest was

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.400
set-up.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:51.469
While Kim Jong-Nam’s mother visited Pyongyang
only occasionally from her home in Moscow,

00:07:51.469 --> 00:07:56.490
and was said not to be particularly ambitious,
Kim Jong-Un’s mother was highly involved

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:01.569
in political life, pushing behind the scenes
for her son’s ascent to power.

00:08:01.569 --> 00:08:06.270
Seeing his side of the family had lost favor,
the eldest son lived an aimless life of parties

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:11.360
in Pyongyang until his father offered him
a deal: Get married and have a child, and

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:17.610
you can leave North Korea - which Kim Jong-Nam
took, moving, with his family, to Macau.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:22.740
The middle child, meanwhile, was considered
too quiet and unmotivated, leaving only the

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:23.970
youngest.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:29.199
Kim Jong-Un, to be clear, was not the perfect
candidate - his mother was born in Japan,

00:08:29.199 --> 00:08:32.889
never legally married to Kim Jong-Il, and
her sister had defected.

00:08:32.889 --> 00:08:37.759
Still, thanks to his mother’s maneuvering,
Un was officially chosen as successor about

00:08:37.759 --> 00:08:42.839
5 months after Kim Jong-Il’s near-fatal
stroke in 2008, after which he had trouble

00:08:42.839 --> 00:08:45.690
moving the left side of his body.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:50.580
Almost nothing was known about the then roughly
25-year-old dictator-in-waiting, who, like

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:57.079
his father, slowly ascended the party until
December 17th, 2011, when Kim Jong-Il, also

00:08:57.079 --> 00:09:00.380
like his father, died of a heart attack.

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:06.160
Both times, outsiders watched the transition
- first, from a militant revolutionary ideologue,

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:11.880
to an awkward film nerd, then to a basketball-loving
28-year-old with about 3 years of experience

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.720
- and waited for the regime to collapse.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.970
Each time they said the country could not
survive without the personality behind the

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:24.529
cult, and each time the transition was incredibly
smooth, and their tenures long.

00:09:24.529 --> 00:09:29.320
At some point, one must accept that, for all
their villainous behavior, the Kim family

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.589
is also extremely skilled, strategically.

00:09:32.589 --> 00:09:38.130
It should come as no surprise, then, that,
as of now, there is no obvious next-in-line,

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:41.579
which could present a serious threat to the
current leadership.

00:09:41.579 --> 00:09:46.250
If tradition continues, as it tends to in
North Korea, power will be inherited by one

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.279
of Kim Jong-Un’s male children.

00:09:48.279 --> 00:09:54.269
Two factors, however, complicate this: First,
of his three reported children, the oldest

00:09:54.269 --> 00:10:00.639
is said to be only 10, which, let’s hope,
is far too young, even by North Korean standards.

00:10:00.639 --> 00:10:05.610
Second, Kim Jong-Un’s physical health is
probably much worse than his predecessors,

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:10.120
meaning there’s a very real chance he could
die before any of his children reach maturity

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.470
- which brings us back to the family tree.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:17.660
Anyone with Kim-family blood, according to
the country’s culture and tradition, is

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:23.630
a potential rival, as evidenced by the assassination
of Kim Jong-Nam in 2017.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:27.590
While returning to his home in Macau, the
eldest brother was attacked and killed at

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:30.779
a check-in counter at the Kuala Lumpur airport.

00:10:30.779 --> 00:10:37.070
Carrying $120,000 in cash, he’s suspected
of being a CIA-informant, and, as evidenced

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.620
by his 12 vials of antidotes, a nervous one.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:45.480
His son - Kim Han-Sol is currently in hiding
- and would probably be extremely wise to

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.089
remain that way.

00:10:47.089 --> 00:10:52.090
The most realistic replacements, however,
come from within the country - the most high-profile

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.620
of which is Kim Jong-Un’s sister, Kim Yo
Jong.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:59.829
When she first appeared in public at her father’s
funeral, so little was known about her that

00:10:59.829 --> 00:11:02.970
some suspected she was Kim Jong-Un’s wife.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:07.350
Since then, she has assumed the very public
role of, essentially, his brother’s assistant

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:13.670
- she can be seen standing behind him at important
meetings and handing him a pen at signings.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:18.139
Many would recognize her face from the 2018
Winter Olympics, where she made waves for

00:11:18.139 --> 00:11:22.740
standing during the South Korean national
anthem, cheering for the unified-Korea flag,

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.600
and inviting the president to meet with her
brother.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:30.730
On one hand, the amount of power she has accumulated
and her physical proximity to Kim Jong-Un

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.600
is a clear sign of trust.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:38.140
But, given that Un had his own uncle executed
by firing squad, what looks like trust could

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:42.029
just as easily be doubt in her ability to
pose a threat...

00:11:42.029 --> 00:11:46.680
While she does have the all-important Kim-family
blood, she would likely struggle to gain support

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:51.779
in the North’s very patriarchal culture
- making her a valuable asset to the current

00:11:51.779 --> 00:11:53.139
leadership.

00:11:53.139 --> 00:11:59.029
Her supposed father-in-law, the well-connected
Choe Ryong Hae - is another possible contender.

00:11:59.029 --> 00:12:03.421
As a member of the party’s standing committee,
central committee, military commission, and

00:12:03.421 --> 00:12:08.199
a deputy of the Supreme People’s Assembly,
Ryong Hae is one of the most powerful senior

00:12:08.199 --> 00:12:10.190
officials in the country.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:15.230
Although he lacks the family blood and, therefore,
also the financial access, he’s had decades

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:21.250
to build and maintain a coalition, which could,
in theory, eventually be used to seize control.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:25.779
That leaves only Kim Jong-Chol, the older
full brother of Kim Jong-Un.

00:12:25.779 --> 00:12:31.730
Chol, reportedly, can be found in one of two
places: in Pyongyang, where he plays guitar,

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:34.259
or wherever Eric Clapton is playing a concert.

00:12:34.259 --> 00:12:38.860
It would seem his father was right, he has
no political ambitions.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.350
Or, like all of this, so it’s thought.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:46.149
The trouble with understanding North Korea
is that so much of what we “know” is based

00:12:46.149 --> 00:12:52.640
on stories told by a select few insiders living
abroad - people like Kenji Fujimoto, formerly

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:57.800
the Kim family sushi chef who watched Kim
Jong-Un and his siblings grow up.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:02.800
With so little information on which to go
on, few opportunities to calibrate our understanding,

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:08.600
and North Korea, itself, usually disinterested
in confirming or denying rumors, the outside

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.870
world faces a tough dilemma:

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:15.930
It would be foolish to totally disregard the
few tidbits of information we do have as unproven

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:21.209
speculation, but, it would also be foolish
to accept them wholeheartedly, and risk being

00:13:21.209 --> 00:13:26.209
misled, as we saw happen with the recent reports
of Kim Jong-Un’s death.

00:13:26.209 --> 00:13:30.660
The next time Kim Jong-Un disappears, we may
learn from this mistake and quickly dismiss

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:31.660
the story.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:36.480
And yet, when he does eventually disappear
from the world for good, that’s exactly

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.750
how it will probably look.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:44.399
When Kim Jong-Il died in December 2011, the
world continued operating as usual, totally

00:13:44.399 --> 00:13:47.420
oblivious, for 51 hours.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:51.731
During that time, the South Korean president
flew to Tokyo, met the Prime Minister, and

00:13:51.731 --> 00:13:52.930
flew back.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:56.620
Its defense minister was in a meeting when
the announcement was finally made.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:14:02.750
Afterward, the Obama administration reluctantly
admitted they were “largely bystanders”

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:07.500
as the guard changed in this notoriously cruel,
nuclear-armed nation.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:12.820
As it turned out, we got lucky - there was
no chaotic struggle for power and 25 million

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:16.569
citizens didn’t come flooding through the
Chinese border.

00:14:16.569 --> 00:14:20.029
Next time, no one knows for sure.

00:14:20.029 --> 00:14:24.820
If, like me, you’re not busy managing the
succession of your dictatorship, I’m willing

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:27.400
to bet you might have a little extra time
at the moment.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:31.579
If you’re going to be stuck indoors, why
not make use of that time to learn something

00:14:31.579 --> 00:14:33.540
